    "body": "### Additional findings\n\nI checked the current `w3c/mdn-spec-links/html.json` and found that this is not limited to `serializable-objects`.\n\nThere are currently multiple HTML fragments for which the same MDN URL occurs more than once in the generated annotation data. Some notable examples are:\n\n- `serializable-objects`: 7 entries for the same MDN article\n- `the-h1,-h2,-h3,-h4,-h5,-and-h6-elements`: 6 entries for `HTML/Element/Heading_Elements`\n- `attr-fe-disabled`: 5 entries for `HTML/Attributes/disabled`\n- `the-readonly-attribute`: 3 entries for `HTML/Attributes/readonly`\n- `link-type-noopener`: 2 entries for `HTML/Link_types/noopener`\n- `link-type-noreferrer`: 2 entries for `HTML/Link_types/noreferrer`\n\nSo the duplicate-panel issue appears to be more general than the `Serializable objects` case.\n\nSome of these entries have identical compatibility data, while others originate from different BCD features with different compatibility data despite sharing the same MDN article. Therefore, blindly deduplicating by MDN URL might not be sufficient; grouping or aggregating entries associated with the same MDN article may need to be considered.\n\nI also found that the malformed-URL problem affects `/docs/Learn/` pages, not just `/docs/Glossary/`.\n\nFor example, the annotation for:\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#client-side-form-validation\n\ncomes from:\n\n```text\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn/Forms/Form_validation\n```\n\nbut Wattsi generates:\n\n```text\nhttps://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Forms/Form_validation\n```\n\nwhich is a 404.\n\nSimilarly, the annotation for:\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#sections\n\ncomes from an MDN `/docs/Learn/HTML/...` page, but is generated as `/docs/Web/HTML/...`, which is also a 404.\n\nThis seems to further support using the complete `mdn_url` supplied by `mdn-spec-links`, rather than reconstructing every MDN URL from a `/docs/Web/` base plus `slug`.",
